47
00:01:54,136 --> 00:01:56,780
And that's where this hooks feature offered

48
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:59,424
by Claude Code can come in handy. The idea

49
00:01:59,424 --> 00:02:01,508
behind Claude Code hooks is simply that you

50
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:04,664
can react to certain events emitted by

51
00:02:04,712 --> 00:02:07,340
Claude Code, for example, that it edited a

52
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:07,629
file,

53
00:02:08,238 --> 00:02:10,737
and you can then run any code of your choice

54
00:02:10,802 --> 00:02:14,056
in reaction to that change. And you can add

55
00:02:14,232 --> 00:02:18,031
hooks in the local settings JSON file that's

56
00:02:18,031 --> 00:02:20,564
not checked into version control, into the

57
00:02:20,564 --> 00:02:21,670
local one that is,

58
00:02:22,247 --> 00:02:24,636
or also in the global one on your system

59
00:02:24,668 --> 00:02:26,672
that's shared across projects. Here I'll use

60
00:02:26,672 --> 00:02:28,675
the local one that is checked into version

61
00:02:28,675 --> 00:02:28,964
control.

62
00:02:29,958 --> 00:02:31,689
There in that JSON

63
00:02:32,266 --> 00:02:34,094
object, you can add a hooks node

64
00:02:34,751 --> 00:02:37,316
and then add as many hooks as you want. And

65
00:02:37,332 --> 00:02:39,950
you do add a new hook by first specifying

66
00:02:39,982 --> 00:02:41,780
the event to which you wanna react. And

67
00:02:41,812 --> 00:02:43,466
attached, you find a link to the official

68
00:02:43,499 --> 00:02:45,843
documentation that lists all hook events to

69
00:02:45,843 --> 00:02:46,823
which you can react.

70
00:02:47,369 --> 00:02:50,500
You, for example, got preToolUse, which is a

71
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:52,556
hook that allows you to execute code

72
00:02:52,909 --> 00:02:56,377
whenever Claude Code is about to use a tool.

73
00:02:56,506 --> 00:02:58,947
And a tool is something like doing web

74
00:02:58,947 --> 00:03:00,810
search or editing a file

75
00:03:01,404 --> 00:03:01,452
or

76
00:03:02,046 --> 00:03:04,358
reading a file. So whenever Claude Code does

77
00:03:04,551 --> 00:03:07,040
anything about that, you could execute some

78
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:07,249
code.

79
00:03:08,243 --> 00:03:10,937
There also are a lot of other events, of

80
00:03:10,969 --> 00:03:13,663
course, for example, also postToolUse.

81
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,308
And that sounds interesting for us here

82
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:18,761
because that is a hook that runs after a

83
00:03:18,825 --> 00:03:20,814
tool has been called. And since, for

84
00:03:20,814 --> 00:03:23,972
example, writing to a file or editing a file

85
00:03:24,117 --> 00:03:26,522
is a tool call, that's what we need to

86
00:03:26,522 --> 00:03:29,696
format a file after it has been edited. So

87
00:03:29,808 --> 00:03:33,272
it's postToolUse and you must write it

88
00:03:33,272 --> 00:03:35,821
exactly as specified in the documentation.

89
00:03:36,302 --> 00:03:38,486
And then this takes an array because you can

90
00:03:38,534 --> 00:03:41,152
of course register multiple hooks, multiple

91
00:03:41,585 --> 00:03:43,865
code snippets that should execute for this

92
00:03:43,994 --> 00:03:44,267
event.

93
00:03:45,198 --> 00:03:46,707
In that array, you have one

94
00:03:47,285 --> 00:03:48,200
object per

95
00:03:48,746 --> 00:03:50,352
code snippet you wanna execute.

96
00:03:50,898 --> 00:03:52,857
And in that code snippet, you then have a

97
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:55,940
matcher which allows you to specify which

98
00:03:56,052 --> 00:03:58,910
tool was used for this hook event. And for

99
00:03:59,007 --> 00:04:01,046
different hook events, the matcher

100
00:04:01,672 --> 00:04:03,743
expects different things. The official

101
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:06,150
documentation is the way to go, of course,

102
00:04:06,471 --> 00:04:08,751
to learn how to react to different hook

103
00:04:08,831 --> 00:04:11,014
input and set up your matcher for different

104
00:04:11,046 --> 00:04:11,303
hooks.

105
00:04:11,929 --> 00:04:15,171
In case of the postToolUse hook, we simply

106
00:04:15,171 --> 00:04:18,687
specify the kind of tools we wanna react to.

107
00:04:18,911 --> 00:04:21,255
So after the use of which tools do we want

108
00:04:21,255 --> 00:04:23,534
to execute some code? And in my case, that's

109
00:04:23,807 --> 00:04:26,295
edit or write, and you would write it like

110
00:04:26,295 --> 00:04:29,072
this. So use the pipe symbol here to

111
00:04:29,522 --> 00:04:31,256
basically say that you have multiple

112
00:04:31,834 --> 00:04:34,531
matching options. So whenever the edit or

113
00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:38,080
write tool was used, I want to do something.

114
00:04:38,674 --> 00:04:41,275
So then you can specify your hooks. Again,

115
00:04:41,404 --> 00:04:43,218
this is an array because you could have

116
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:45,546
multiple actions that should happen whenever

117
00:04:45,739 --> 00:04:48,404
the edit or write tools were used. And you

118
00:04:48,404 --> 00:04:50,845
have one object per thing that should then

119
00:04:50,877 --> 00:04:51,246
happen.

120
00:04:52,001 --> 00:04:54,474
And in here you then have the type.

121
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:57,989
Type is command, agent, or prompt. And the 2

